    "title": "After Jackson Twp. woman finds love, how to watch 'Age of Attraction' reunion",
    "text": "Updated April 1, 2026, 7:02 p.m. ETThe conclusion of Netflix's unscripted experimental romance series, \"Age of Attraction,\" is here but the reunion won't stream on NetflixOn the viral dating series, a take on the popular dating show \"Love Is Blind,\" candidates are matched on \"chemistry, compatibility, and an undeniable spark\" while banning one question: \"How old are you?\" As the final fallouts arrives, viewers will need to turn elsewhere for answers.Vanessa Drozda, a 1993 Louisville High School graduate, happened to be one of the people who found love on the show.Here's how to watch the \"Age of Attraction\" reunion, which airs on Wednesday, April 1.How to watch the 'Age of Attraction' reunionThe \"Age of Attraction\" reunion premieres exclusively on \"The Viall Files\" YouTube channel at 7 p.m. ET.Who are the hosts of 'Age of Attraction'?\"Age of Attraction\" is hosted by content creators Nick Viall and Natalie Joy. The couple, who host the popular \"The Viall Files\" podcast, are 44 and 26, respectively.Before their marriage in 2024, Viall was a contestant on Seasons 10 and 11 of \"The Bachelorette\" and Season 3 of \"Bachelor in Paradise.\" He also was the \"Bachelor\" on Season 21 of the series.Is Season One still streaming on Netflix?All eight episodes are available to binge on Netflix.Episode One: \"Is Age Just a Number?\"Episode Two: \"Healthy? Probably Not. Fun? Yes.\"Episode Three: \"He's The Same Age As My Parents\"Episode Four: \"A 27 Year Old Should Be Like An Energizer Bunny\"Episode Five: \"The Power of Life and Death Is In The Tongue\"Episode Six: \"Family Matters\"Episode Seven: \"Can You Tell Us His Age?\"Episode Eight: \"Commitment Day\"Will there be an 'Age of Attraction' Season 2?Yes. The show has been greenlit for Season Two.“We love concepts that are impossible to look away from, and 'Age of Attraction' nailed that from day one,” executive producers Jennifer O’Connell and Rebecca Quinn said, according to Netflix.“It’s messy, it’s real, and that’s what makes it fun to watch. Huge thanks to Netflix for embracing this dating experiment with us,\" O’Connell and Quinn added.Season One premiered on the streaming platform on Wednesday, March 11.Contributing: Greta Cross, USA TODAYTaylor Ardrey is a news reporter for USA TODAY. You can reach her at tardrey@usatodayco.com.",
